Reason: tile_exists, tile_delete, tile_set_alpha, tile_get_background and tile_set_scale each found their tile by
walking the room's whole tile array. AM2R's oTilesRandomAlpha calls tile_set_alpha for every tile in its list every
step, so in rooms like rm_a5a08 that was quadratic: ~4.7 ms a frame (emulated, GML profiler). Tile ids now map to
their first index in the array, built on first use and rebuilt when the room, its array or its length changes or
tile_add / tile_delete / tile_layer_delete(_at) edit it. A hit is confirmed by the id at that index; a miss falls back
to the old walk (and marks the index out of date if the walk finds it); a room whose tiles repeat an id keeps the
walk. Every lookup returns the index the walk returned.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

--- a/src/vm_builtins.c
+++ b/src/vm_builtins.c
